{
  "storyId": "B-9f2c",
  "name": "graph-story-dossier",
  "title": "Migrate the graph story dossier page and add a --story deep-link flag to the graph command",
  "description": "Port the per-story dossier page from the upstream proof-or-stop-graph repository (commits 4c3bde0, 7ecad9a, a0b14da, 1536588, all landed after the 10b5921 migration point already mirrored here) into packages/graph, and expose it from the CLI. The dossier is a full-window mission-control page for ONE story: a finding map, the seven-phase lifecycle loop, a dependency web, checklist/outcome panels, a findings feed, a dispatch swarm, a pulse chart and a wire log, all derived client-side from the existing /api/story detail. It has its own URL /story/<id>, served by the same HTTP shell as /. Upstream files: a new src/shells/web/dossier.js of 1119 lines, plus edits to app.css, app.js, app.body.html, io/http.ts, scripts/build-web.mjs and README.md. On top of the straight port, add a --story=<id> flag to the existing proof-or-stop graph command so the browser opens http://localhost:<port>/story/<id> directly instead of /. An unknown story id must be rejected BEFORE the server starts listening, following the precedent already set for --root in packages/main/src/handlers/graph.ts, where an unresolvable value is refused rather than silently serving an empty view.",
